% \subsection{Compatibility}\label{sec:compat}
% These options decide which commands physunits defines, so they only work
% when the package is loaded, not with \cs{physunitssetup}.
% \begin{description}
% \item[\texttt{disable}] A comma-separated list of command names, given without the backslash, for example \verb|disable={solarmass, ly}|. The listed commands are not defined, so that a document or class can define its own commands with these names. Commands that physunits builds from a disabled command still work; for example \cs{kmps} still works with \verb|disable={meter}|. The option can be given more than once; the lists are combined.
