% \subsection{Defining the public commands}
% \changes{v1.3.0}{2026/11/24}{All units are defined under internal names and made public at the end of the package, so that the \texttt{disable} and \texttt{skip-defined} options can leave out any of them.}
% Every unit, prefix and other command is defined above under an internal
% name, \cs{physunits@u@}\meta{name}, and the commands refer to one another
% only by these internal names. Here each public name is defined to call its
% internal command, unless it was disabled. A public name that already exists
% is left alone with \texttt{skip-defined}; otherwise it is an error, as
% before, except for the commands that were always declared with
